shUMEM (CLAUDE.md 21.4): let PCM skip its per-socket "speedup trick".

PCM moves its own thread, on every sample, onto socketRefCore[s] (the last
CPU of socket s) before reading that socket's uncore MSRs. On sm220u with the
NIC on socket 0 that CPU is an isolated polling lcore (p1q7), so each sample
preempted it for up to ~190 us. With PCM_NO_SPEEDUP_AFFINITY set the thread
stays on its housekeeping CPU and the reads reach the core by IPI; without it
PCM behaves as upstream. Made against intel/pcm 8574a1f; applied with
patch -p1 by setup/dev-environment.sh dut.

